{"chapter-slug":"rw7-07","paragraph":977,"wording":"[Mayor]","event":"named","holder-quote":"Cetris Duiland nodded, shuffling his papers. Erin stared around. Most of the people on Celum’s side looked some measure of triumphant, although Trent was looking worried as he stared at Octavia.","id":"d625f272-72a0-5f62-b6ac-054d0599223c"}
{"chapter-slug":"rw7-07","paragraph":986,"wording":"[Mayor]","event":"named","holder-quote":"Erin muttered back. She saw Cetris turn his head. But the [Mayor] said nothing more. Erin nodded","id":"db53657d-f038-51d4-b04b-5f1ff3da9706"}
{"chapter-slug":"rw7-07","paragraph":1006,"wording":"[Mayor]","event":"named","holder-quote":"She looked at Cetris Duiland. The [Mayor] stared at her. Guilds were one thing. Inns were one thing. Even the threat of monster attacks.","id":"68bcccf4-d883-5425-8ad5-9fa0298fe753"}
{"chapter-slug":"rw7-07","paragraph":1012,"wording":"[Mayor]","event":"named","holder-quote":"Montressa glared at Cetris. But she and Octavia were already sitting back down. The other Guildmasters and [Innkeepers] were returning to their places as well. Cetris nodded at Montressa.","id":"15172f2f-ffa8-5181-a2f5-31ea8932cc08"}
